/RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:11.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">ASCII is the acronym for the A</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">merican Standard Code for I</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">nformation Interchange. It is a c</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">ode for representing 128 E</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">nglish characters as n</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">umbers, with each letter a</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">ssigned a number from 0 to 1</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">27. For example, the ASCII c</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">ode for uppercase M is 77</span></p></body>)
/Q 0
/T (Faisal Kaleem)
/Contents (ASCII is the acronym for the American Standard Code for Information Interchange. It is a code for representing 128 English characters as numbers, with each letter assigned a number from 0 to 127. For example, the ASCII code for uppercase M is 77)
/Type /Annot
/Subtype /FreeText
/Rotate 0
/DA ( /Helvetica 9 Tf)
/CA 1
/NM (130d5f45-7130-4466-becb-64d5aab1a268)
>>
