/RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:11.0.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">use of LODS; pick the data, do the&#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">&#x20;processing&#x20;</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">&#x20;</span><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">and then use STOS &#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">instruction to do block processing.&#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">&#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">In string printing , use LODS to&#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">&#x20;read a character of the string, &#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">and use STOS to write it on&#x0A;</span></p><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:left;font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;color:#0000FF;font-family:Helvetica">&#x20;video memory.</span></p></body>)
